<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Basil Read turns profitable at year-end.</title>
<headline>Basil Read turns profitable at year-end.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  16.9 profit vs 31.2 loss</p>
<p>    - headline		16.9 profit vs 15.5 loss</p>
<p>    Net profit		9.30 prifit vs 14.50 loss</p>
<p>Pre-tax		   9.64 profit vs 14.34 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.34	  vs 0.16</p>
<p>    Interest received     1.74	  vs 2.19 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  583.61	vs 388.40</p>
<p>Full name: Basil Read Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil	   vs 7.31 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - The engineering to building firm said the figures came after four consecutive years of losses. It added the turnaround was attributable to a policy of establishing specialised technical and commercial departments.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
